# Intent: The asset store, the pure logic (owner decision 17; design docs/plan/installed-set.md sections B and G): one store of flash for every kind of installed asset. The typed 128 byte asset header (MPAH1: kind, name, version, body length and SHA-256, board id, minimum build, a license id and an author id) with its checks, every refusal in plain words with a Spanish twin; a directory ring of 8 sectors (the newest valid sector wins, each change wears the next sector); entries that carry the content id (first 8 bytes of the body hash), the active mark and up to four dependency ids; atomic install (data first, read back and hash, then the directory flips) that replaces in place without touching the old run; swap (a change of the active item, one directory write), remove (one directory write); first fit from a rotating start so wear spreads; reference counts computed from the directory, never stored. No device code uses it yet: the tools and the game-pack consumer are the next patch.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_assets_core.h (ours)
# Check after a flash: none (a pure core; the host test cuts the power at every flash step of an install, a replace, a swap and a remove and checks that the old set or the new set is whole after each cut).
# Kconfig: none
# Memory cost: none (nothing includes the core yet; when the device layer lands it holds one 4,096 byte PSRAM scratch sector while an install runs and a directory of about 4 KB in PSRAM).

diff --git a/firmware/main/hal/maipai_assets_core.h b/firmware/main/hal/maipai_assets_core.h
